<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin I of Sicily</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1374–<a href="/years/1409">1409</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Martin the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin I, called Martin the Younger, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from 1390 to 1409, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon">Martin I of Aragon</a>. He restored royal authority over the Sicilian barons, and in 1409 he won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sanluri">Battle of Sanluri</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, breaking the power of Arborea, but died of fever at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cagliari">Cagliari</a> weeks later. His death without a legitimate heir ended the separate Sicilian line, and the island passed to the Crown of Aragon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-i-of-sicily.jpg" alt="Martin I of Sicily" width="244" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martin1Sicilsky.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
